+- The display is flashed, and its console read, over its own USB-C (`testbench/WIRING.md:75`; `docs/Link.md:19-23`). The link-cable supply blocks reverse current, so the display's USB-C feeds nothing into the IO board; the part is TPS259474ARPWR (R5). Link power reaches the display's USB-C VBUS: the display joins that VBUS to its 5 V net with only a TVS (transient-voltage-suppression) diode to ground (V80, found in FU-2I). The owner states it as a current limitation: no host or charger on the display's native USB-C while the link cable carries 5 V (V329).
