+The servo rail clamp of V315 and V316 sits behind an ideal diode on each of
+the 3 servo rails and on the adjustable supply's output. An ideal-diode
+controller and its MOSFET keep back-fed current from the converter. The
+op-amp switches a load resistor across the rail once the rail exceeds the
+voltage before the MOSFET by 0.1 V. The controller has no part (V321), so the circuit
+rests on a missing part. A hard-braking servo at the top set point may cut an
+HV (high-voltage) port off, which reconnects by the comparator's hysteresis
+(V322, a current limitation).
 
