+
+**Servo current sample period**, assumed, beside the servo current abort and
+I²C bus timing on the measurement buses: 5 ms, a 200 Hz current sensor. The
+measurement coprocessor reads each INA3221 and checks the 3.0 A ceiling at
+every sample; the INA3221 refreshes its 3 channels in 3.63 ms at most in
+shunt-only mode, so each channel gives a fresh value at every sample. Why:
+the tree does not state the period; `docs/Servo.md:35` says "checked at every
+sample", and the host test models the sensor at 5 ms
+(`test/host/test_servo_limit.c:19`). The 20 ms BENCH period belongs to the
+motor monitor's reading, not to the port current sample.
 
